\item R (mzLibR): \code{stats_fit_latent_mixed}
}
}
\section{Since}{
Wire protocol 1; pyMzLib 0.7.0; mzLibRust not yet shipped; mzLibR not yet shipped.
}
\references{
\itemize{
\item \href{https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1993.10594284}{doi:10.1080/01621459.1993.10594284}: generalized linear mixed models, the class of model this verb fits: a latent linear predictor with a random intercept, observed through a binomial link (Breslow and Clayton, J Am Stat Assoc 88:9, 1993)
\item \href{https://doi.org/10.1093/biomet/81.3.624}{doi:10.1093/biomet/81.3.624}: adaptive Gauss-Hermite quadrature, centred at the integrand's mode and scaled by its curvature, which mzLib uses to integrate the counted samples (Liu and Pierce, Biometrika 81:624, 1994)
\item \href{https://doi.org/10.18637/jss.v067.i01}{doi:10.18637/jss.v067.i01}: lme4's lmer and glmer (nAGQ 25), the references mzLib's fits are held to (Bates, Maechler, Bolker and Walker, J Stat Softw 67:1, 2015)
\item \href{https://doi.org/10.32614/RJ-2017-066}{doi:10.32614/RJ-2017-066}: glmmTMB, whose Laplace-approximated REML mzLib's REML follows and whose fits with run scatter are a reference (Brooks et al., R Journal 9:378, 2017)
\item \href{https://doi.org/10.1093/biomet/58.3.545}{doi:10.1093/biomet/58.3.545}: restricted maximum likelihood, the default estimator (Patterson and Thompson, Biometrika 58:545, 1971)
\item \href{https://doi.org/10.1111/j.2517-6161.1948.tb00014.x}{doi:10.1111/j.2517-6161.1948.tb00014.x}: the beta-binomial distribution, which a link with overdispersion gives a count cell (Skellam, J R Stat Soc B 10:257, 1948)
}
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{stats_fit_link}} for the link, \code{\link{stats_fit_mixed}} when every sample is measured
}
\examples{

\dontshow{.mzlibr_example <- mzLibR:::replay_bridge_start()}
# mzLib's own reference input: 16 simulated features, 23 samples in 8 animals, every sample
# counted, read through the link (-0.4, 0.6, 0.3) with a depth term; and lme4's glmer() fit of it
# (25-point adaptive quadrature, maximum likelihood), which this package ships.
data <- system.file("extdata", "stats", package = "mzLibR")
fit <- stats_fit_latent_mixed(file.path(data, "lnmm_reference_design.tsv"),
  file.path(data, "lnmm_reference_groups.tsv"), c("Intercept", "trait", "x"),
  link = c(-0.4, 0.6, 0.3), counts = file.path(data, "lnmm_link_counts.tsv"),
  depth = file.path(data, "lnmm_link_depth.tsv"),
  residual_variance = file.path(data, "lnmm_link_residual_variance.tsv"), estimator = "ml")
fit
trait <- fit$records[fit$records$coefficient == "trait", ]
glmer <- read.delim(file.path(data, "lnmm_counted_fit.tsv"))
glmer <- glmer[glmer$link == "link" & glmer$method == "ML", ]
# Every trait estimate is within 1e-5 standard errors of glmer's:
max(abs(trait$estimate - glmer$b1) / glmer$se1) < 1e-5
\dontshow{mzLibR:::replay_bridge_stop(.mzlibr_example)}
}
